let __v_244 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"Learn to make one loaf of bread by hand: flour, water, yeast, salt, an hour of rising, and the house does the rest. The first one is always a bit wonky and nobody minds.\",\"Swim outside once - a lake, a lido, the sea in October - with a friend and a towel waiting. Twenty seconds is enough to know you did it.\",\"See a band you have never heard of in a small room on a week night. A cheap ticket, no expectations, and it is the best way to find music you keep.\",\"Take one night away on your own: a train, a cheap room, a book. It is a different kind of trip from a holiday with people, and easier than it sounds.\",\"Watch the sunrise on purpose once: check the time, set an alarm, take a flask. One early start buys you a morning you will talk about for years.\",\"Learn to change a tyre and check your oil before you have to. Ten minutes of practice on your own drive beats an hour on a hard shoulder in the rain.\",\"Eat in a restaurant by yourself, with a book, once. Nobody is looking, and it is the most peaceful hour you can buy for the price of a lunch.\",\"Post a real letter to somebody who will not expect it - a grandparent, an old teacher, a friend who moved away. It lands differently from a message.\",\"Plant something you can eat and keep it alive to the plate. Herbs on a windowsill count, and one tomato plant teaches you more than a book does.\",\"Go to a match of a sport you know nothing about and sit with the crowd. Someone will explain the rules before half time, and the noise is the point.\",\"Give a morning to something local - a food bank, a park clean-up, a repair cafe. One morning with no commitment afterwards, and you will meet people you would never otherwise meet.\",\"Cook the same dish once a week until you can do it without the recipe. Everyone should own one dinner, and six goes is usually enough.\",\"Draw something badly on purpose, and keep it. Being a beginner at something for an afternoon is good for you.\",\"Catch a train to a town an hour away with no plan for the day: walk it, have lunch, come home. The having-no-plan is the good bit.\",\"Take a class where you make something with your hands - pottery, woodwork, knitting, welding. A thing that stays made is a rare sort of satisfaction.\",\"Sleep outside once: a tent in a friend's garden, a campsite, a bothy. You will remember the night, not how well you slept.\",\"Learn ten words of a language before you go somewhere that speaks it. Shopkeepers forgive a lot for one honest attempt.\",\"Ask an older relative to tell you about their childhood and record it on your phone. It is the cheapest history you will ever collect.\"]}")?;
