let __v_897 = Value::from("Plan a kitchen round the three points that get used most - the sink, the hob and the fridge: any two of them want 1.2 to 2.7 metres between them, the sink wants a clear 600mm of worktop on each side, and the hob wants space to put a pan down on the right and nothing flammable beside it. Then list what you need before what you want: deep drawers beat a bottom cupboard, a socket every metre of worktop, a tall cupboard for the ironing board and the hoover. Mark where the pipes, the soil stack and the door swing are before you fall in love with a layout, because moving a drain is most of a kitchen's cost. Tape the outline on the floor and walk it for a week before you order.");
frame.store("_KITCHEN_PLAN", __v_897.clone())?;
let __v_898 = Value::from("Plan a bathroom round the soil pipe: the toilet has to stay where the drain already is unless you raise the floor for a new one, so put the toilet and the bath first and the basin where there is wall for it. A bath needs 1.7m and a shower 900mm square, and leave 700mm clear in front of the basin and 600mm beside the toilet. Decide the shower before the tiles, because a wet room floor has to fall to a drain and a screen cannot be added later, and set the shower valve about 1.1m off the floor so nobody has to reach. A bathroom also needs an extractor that moves about 15 litres a second, or the paint and the grout will go.");
frame.store("_BATHROOM_PLAN", __v_898.clone())?;
let __v_899 = Value::from("Plan a utility room round the machines and the water: the washing machine and the dryer want an outside wall for the vent and the plumbing, a sink close to the drain, and a worktop over the appliances at about 900mm so there is a surface to fold on. Leave 600mm clear in front of every door you have to open, put the boiler behind a cupboard you can still get into, and keep a shelf at eye height for powder, pegs and the iron - it is the walk-through clutter, not the size of the room, that makes a utility room useless.");
frame.store("_UTILITY_PLAN", __v_899.clone())?;
